The bundled, unmodified optional Frontier Master Daemon originates from
MiSTerOrganize/MiSTer_Frontier at commit
a7c61e0a000d9dfd40235e638229e06a603534d5, under GPL version 3.
https://github.com/MiSTerOrganize/MiSTer_Frontier
An existing Frontier installation is preserved by the TIC-80 install script.

The staged MiSTer emu interface, platform framework, and PLL originate from
MiSTerOrganize/MiSTer_PICO-8 at commit
72cb0405417d506c33e59ab51c1a374fc4db649e, including MiSTer Menu work by
Alexey Melnikov (Sorgelig) and the respective authors named in source headers.
https://github.com/MiSTerOrganize/MiSTer_PICO-8
Original source headers and licenses are retained in the staged build.
The local ascal.vhd override retains TEMLIB's original header and changes only
the horizontal divider's first two arithmetic stages to compute their second-step
candidates in parallel. Its outputs and pipeline latency are preserved.
The local i2s.v override derives from the same pinned platform serializer.
It keeps BCLK running during reset and latches short reset requests until
data/LRCLK can be cleared at the normal safe data-update phase.

