The console/editor build also uses the pinned zip (kuba--/zip), argparse
(cofyc/argparse), jsmn (zserge/jsmn) and blip-buf wave writer sources, retaining
their original license headers and repository license files.
Studio staging exposes its existing popup for platform messages and guards
the FFT initialization when built without a microphone capture backend.
Staging also completes failed hash downloads, validates cartridge caches,
closes networking before callback owners, and releases the original PNG-save
buffer before replacing it with the encoded image. The asynchronous HTTP
transport uses the system curl executable with its original license.
assets/cacert.pem is Mozilla CA data extracted by curl, under MPL version 2.0;
see assets/LICENSE.cacert and assets/cacert-source.json for its license and
pinned provenance. The bundle is used without changing the system trust store.

Build staging retains upstream source/license headers while correcting the
pinned native-cart serializer's returned length for CHUNK_LANG. Integration
adapters isolate global interpreter state for Python, Janet, WASM, Wren,
Ruby and Forth; upstream API implementations remain in the pinned checkout.
The public-player adapter retains tick callback data and the clock epoch for
each VM's lifetime; the pinned implementation recreated it on the stack.
The core-close adapter releases the original RAM allocation after VM cleanup,
including when WASM redirects the active RAM pointer into module memory.
Build staging closes partially initialized VMs before discarding their pointers.
The WASM module adapter frees its owned memory/table export and import names; the
included wasm3 implementation retains its original source and license.
The staged Python easing aliases copy their values before dictionary insertion
can rehash and invalidate the original value pointers.
The staged s7 source omits four unused permanent string allocations; its
original implementation and license are retained.
The MiniScript callback adapter temporarily clears/restores the main harness's
yield flag around synchronous SCN, BDR and MENU callbacks.
The integration's cartridge-file decoder uses the pinned libpng and zlib
dependencies to validate PNG containers and extract a bounded native cartridge;
live execution bypasses upstream's unchecked PNG read callback.
